    "/api/v1/conversations/{cid}/escalate": {
      "post": {
        "description": "docs/SPEC.md \u00a77. [SECURITY] Mirrors app/chat/routes.py's own\n`get_conversation_messages()` for the cross-tenant/cross-visitor\n404 shape EXACTLY -- the identical attack surface (another\nvisitor's cid same tenant; another tenant's cid; a cid that does\nnot exist at all) must be indistinguishable here too, proven by\n`tests/test_handoff_routes.py`'s own direct side-by-side response\ncomparison, not three separate \"it's 404\" assertions trusted to\nmatch.",
        "operationId": "submit_escalation_api_v1_conversations__cid__escalate_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "cid",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Cid",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EscalationRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EscalationResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Submit Escalation"
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/conversations/{cid}/messages": {
      "get": {
        "description": "docs/SPEC.md \u00a710: \"history, showing completed turns only\".\n\nReads the real LangGraph checkpoint via `read_state()` (the same\nguarded entry point `/chat` itself uses) -- no separate `messages`\ntable exists (docs/SPEC.md \u00a715's own data model names none). \"Completed\nturns only\": if the thread's own LAST message is a `HumanMessage` with\nno following `AIMessage` (a turn that crashed, timed out, or is still\ngenuinely in flight), it is dropped from the response rather than shown\nhalf-finished.\n\n**Real, named limitation, not silently worked around**: only `role`\nand `text` are returned, never `citations` -- `AgentState.citations`\n(app/agent/graph.py) is a per-turn OVERWRITE field (Task 3.4.e, reset\nevery turn by design), so only the MOST RECENT turn's own citations\nare ever recoverable from current graph state at all; reconstructing\nevery past turn's own citations would need a dedicated, independently-\npersisted messages table, which is a real architectural decision\n(whether/when to build one) this task does not make unilaterally --\nsee PROJECT_SPEC.md's own new \u00a79 marker.",
        "operationId": "get_conversation_messages_api_v1_conversations__cid__messages_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "cid",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Cid",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConversationMessagesResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Conversation Messages"
      }
    },
